    {
      "passage_id": "2e2a9fa7-e1c4-47cd-ae25-acb7634cc72a",
      "slug": "scanning-highest-mountains",
      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "# Scanning — The World's Highest Mountains\n\nWhat is the highest place a person can stand on our planet? The answer lies among the giant peaks of Asia, where the tallest mountains on Earth reach far into the sky.\n\nThe most famous of these is Mount Everest, which sits in the Himalayas, on the border between Nepal and China. Everest stands at 8,849 metres, making it the highest mountain on Earth. The summit was first reached in 1953, when Edmund Hillary from New Zealand and Tenzing Norgay, a Sherpa guide, climbed to the very top.\n\nThe second highest mountain is K2, which rises to 8,611 metres on the border between Pakistan and China. Although it is a little lower than Everest, K2 is far more difficult and has earned the nickname the Savage Mountain because it is so dangerous to climb.\n\nIn third place is Kangchenjunga, which reaches 8,586 metres on the border between Nepal and India. Long ago, before careful measurements were taken, people believed this peak was the highest mountain in the whole world.\n\nAll of these mountains belong to a small group known as the \"eight-thousanders\" — the only fourteen peaks on Earth that rise above 8,000 metres. The air at such heights is thin and cold, so climbing them is one of the hardest challenges a person can take on.\n\n---\n\n*Practice tip: When you scan, move your eyes quickly over the text to find key words, numbers, or names. You do not need to read every word.*",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "So sánh nhất ('the highest/second highest') là từ khóa scan trong bảng số liệu — đối chiếu với cột 'Height' để điền đúng số (8,849).",
            "point": "So sánh nhất (superlative) với 'the …-est'",
            "review": "So sánh nhất tính từ ngắn: the + adj + -est. Tính từ dài: the most + adj. Luôn có 'the' đứng trước.",
            "example": "Everest stands at 8,849 metres, making it **the highest mountain** on Earth.",
            "analysis": "'the highest mountain' = so sánh nhất của tính từ ngắn 'high' (high→highest), luôn đi với mạo từ 'the'. 'making it…' là cụm phân từ rút gọn nêu hệ quả (= and this makes it…)."
          },
          {
            "tip": "'Although' báo hai ý trái chiều trong cùng câu — đọc kỹ cả hai vế để không nhầm dữ kiện khi scan (K2 thấp hơn NHƯNG khó hơn).",
            "point": "Liên từ nhượng bộ 'Although' + so sánh hơn",
