    {
      "passage_id": "a47dc67a-2ea3-4a0d-b2cb-345bfd8b4b36",
      "slug": "skimming-leonardo-da-vinci",
      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "**A**  Leonardo da Vinci was born in 1452 in a small town near the village of Vinci,\nin what is now Italy. As a teenager he was sent to the busy city of Florence, where\nhe trained in the workshop of the artist Andrea del Verrocchio. There he learned to\npaint, to sculpt and to work with metal, and his unusual skill was noticed early.\n\n**B**  Despite his fame, Leonardo finished surprisingly few paintings. He was a\nperfectionist who was easily pulled away by new interests, and he often left a work\nhalf-done to begin another. Fewer than twenty paintings by him survive today, and some\nof those were never truly completed.\n\n**C**  Much of his genius lived in his notebooks. Leonardo filled thousands of pages\nwith sketches, plans and questions, writing his notes from right to left in a kind of\nmirror writing. He drew flying machines, bridges and the human body long before such\nideas were common, though most of these designs were never built in his lifetime.\n\n**D**  One small portrait made him famous around the world: the Mona Lisa. Painted in\nthe early sixteenth century, it is admired for the woman's mysterious smile and the\nsoft, lifelike shadows. Today it hangs in the Louvre in Paris, where millions of\nvisitors come to see it each year.\n\n**E**  Above all, Leonardo was endlessly curious. He did not simply accept how things\nlooked; he asked why birds could fly, how water moved and how the muscles of the body\nworked. For Leonardo, art and science were never separate — both began with careful\nobservation and a question.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "'who' nối thông tin mô tả về người — khi câu dài, tách mệnh đề 'who…' ra để tìm động từ chính của chủ ngữ.",
            "point": "Mệnh đề quan hệ xác định với 'who' (chỉ người)",
            "review": "Mệnh đề quan hệ xác định chỉ người: N (người) + who + V… , KHÔNG dấu phẩy. 'who' làm chủ ngữ thì sau nó là động từ chia thì.",
            "example": "He was a perfectionist **who was** easily pulled away by new interests.",
            "analysis": "'who' thay cho 'a perfectionist' và làm chủ ngữ của mệnh đề quan hệ; theo sau là động từ 'was'. Không có dấu phẩy vì là mệnh đề xác định, cần thiết để mô tả loại người mà Leonardo là. (Trong mệnh đề này còn có dạng bị động 'was pulled away'.)"
