    {
      "passage_id": "71de99b0-ff37-4d97-b5b8-1138529cd5c1",
      "slug": "tfng-the-benefits-of-reading",
      "library": "l2_skill",
      "source_body_markdown": "Many people treat reading as a pleasant hobby, something to fill a quiet evening, yet a growing body of research suggests that the habit shapes the mind in ways that reach far beyond simple enjoyment. The benefits, it turns out, are surprisingly practical.\n\nThe clearest gain is language. People who read often tend to build a larger vocabulary than those who seldom open a book, because printed text uses a wider and richer range of words than everyday speech. Wide reading is, in fact, among the surest ways to grow one's vocabulary, and a strong vocabulary supports almost every kind of study.\n\nA second benefit is harder to measure but no less real. When readers follow invented characters through a story, they are quietly practising the skill of imagining how other people think and feel. Several researchers argue that reading fiction can strengthen empathy, training the mind to see the world through eyes that are not its own.\n\nReading also calms the body. In one widely cited study, just six minutes of quiet reading was enough to reduce stress, slowing the heart rate and easing the tension in tired muscles. For some readers, a book at the end of the day works rather like a short walk or a few minutes of music.\n\nNone of this means that reading can solve every problem, and the size of each effect may vary from person to person. Even so, the evidence suggests that the simple act of opening a book offers rewards well worth the time it takes.",
      "expected_metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "So sánh hơn hay bị bẫy ở True/False khi câu hỏi đảo chiều so sánh (A hơn B → B hơn A); luôn xác định ai/cái gì 'hơn'.",
            "point": "So sánh hơn với '-er than' / 'larger than'",
            "review": "So sánh hơn: tính từ ngắn + -er + than (larger than, richer than); tính từ dài + more + than. 'those who…' = nhóm người làm việc gì.",
            "example": "People who read often tend to build a **larger** vocabulary **than** those who seldom open a book.",
            "analysis": "Tính từ ngắn 'large' thêm -r thành 'larger', đi với 'than' để so sánh hai nhóm: người đọc nhiều >< người ít đọc. 'those' = 'the people' (đại từ thay danh từ số nhiều) tránh lặp từ. Đây là so sánh hơn cơ bản."
          },
          {
            "tip": "'because' chỉ quan hệ nhân–quả trực tiếp — phần sau 'because' là lý do, thường được hỏi ở câu suy luận cause-effect.",
            "point": "Mệnh đề trạng ngữ chỉ nguyên nhân với 'because'",
